{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>If you are sincere, etc.</b> This may be explained along the lines of what they of blessed memory said in the Yerushalmi, chapter 8 of Terumot (4:11), and this is its language: It is taught — a group of people traveling on the road were met by gentiles who said to them: Give us one of you and we will kill him, and if not we will kill all of you — even if all of them are killed they must not surrender a single soul of Israel. If they designated one for them, etc., they must surrender him, etc. — end of quote. And this is what he said, <b>if you are sincere</b>, meaning you yourselves know whether the truth is with you. <b>One of your brothers</b>, meaning one from among you, and they did not designate him for them. <b>Let him be bound</b> — for there is no fear of death to say let them all be killed rather than surrender him. And upon close examination the verse intends to say that if they are not sincere they have no license in law to leave one of them, for when their words are not scrutinized, the law of a spy applies and he is liable to death, and they would be as though designating him from now to die — and the law is not so, but rather let them all be killed and let them not surrender a single soul from among them. And do not raise a difficulty: do we not find that he took Shimon, and if so it is as though they designated him? This is not so, for perhaps they themselves designated this one from among them." "<b>Or</b> it is possible that after they agreed together to have one of them taken, he preempted and chose Shimon, for the reason that he is the counterpart (zugo) of Levi, and he separated their bundle."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "The Yerushalmi citation '(ד:יא)' appears to reference Yerushalmi Terumot 8:1 (corresponding to the passage about surrendering one soul to save many); the 'ד' may be a misprint for chapter 'ח', already noted by the author as 'פרק ח׳'."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:05.081342123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}